RoboTwin
    https://github.com/RoboTwin-Platform/RoboTwin
    Provides the simulator, tasks, assets, data collection and the ACT / DP
    policy trees. Every path in this repository mirrors a RoboTwin path.

Modified files and the scope of each change:

    policy/ACT/imitate_episodes.py
        adds the three distillation terms (compute_distillation_loss),
        multi-site loss accumulation, teacher loading and the forward hook
        that exposes the supervised block. training loop otherwise unchanged.

    policy/ACT/detr/models/backbone.py
        adds the trainable-visual-set selector (unfreeze_blocks), timm ViT
        backbones with configurable patch grids, and an optional readout
        pooling switch. resnet path unchanged.

    policy/ACT/detr/main.py
        adds two arguments: --backbone_type, --backbone_image_size.

    policy/ACT/act_policy.py
        removes the auxiliary learned distillation projection.

    policy/ACT/constants.py
        reads task definitions from SIM_TASK_CONFIGS.json.

    policy/ACT/utils.py, process_data.py
        carries ground-truth segmentation through the episode pipeline.

    policy/ACT/eval.sh, run_distill_arm.sh, run_freeze_ablation.sh,
    run_eval_arm.sh
        arm selection, task-config threading, checkpoint naming.

    policy/DP/diffusion_policy/model/vision/dp_vit.py
        ViT visual encoder for Diffusion Policy.

    policy/DP/diffusion_policy/model/vision/dp_distill.py
        the same distillation objective for Diffusion Policy. new file.

    policy/DP/diffusion_policy/workspace/robotworkspace.py
        wires the distillation loss into the DP training workspace.

    policy/DP/diffusion_policy/model/common/lr_scheduler.py
        schedule adjustment for the distillation run.

    policy/DP/diffusion_policy/config/robot_dp_vit_14.yaml
        config for the ViT-backbone DP runs.

    envs/camera/camera.py
        records per-actor and per-mesh segmentation alongside RGB.

    Segmentation/
        the teacher. unet.py is an Attention U-Net; dataset.py, train.py,
        evaluate.py and extract_data.py are written for this work.

